      "ownershipVehicle": "Axium LTC Limited Partnership",
      "description": "Axium Extendicare LTC II LP is the Ontario-Manitoba long-term-care ownership platform that succeeded AXR Operating (National) LP and the relevant portion of the former Revera-Axium joint venture. At June 30, 2026, it owned 26 operating homes with 3,502 beds; Axium held 85% through Axium LTC Limited Partnership, while Extendicare held a 15% managed interest and operated the homes. The platform serves residents requiring provincially regulated long-term care and receives operating, management and procurement services from Extendicare. Arbour Heights is a 174-bed Kingston home beneath this platform, not a separate PortCo. The original venture formed in 2017 at 75% Axium and 25% Revera, separated its western assets into an AgeCare-Axium venture in 2022, and became Axium Extendicare LTC II LP when Extendicare acquired Revera's remaining 15% Ontario-Manitoba interest in 2023. No later platform sale or signed pending ownership transfer was identified through August 18, 2026.",
